This is coming from our District Ranger Michele Holman if we every run into=
 this, (it has not been an issue here but good info).

People have the right to film public employees performing job duties on pub=
lic property.  If you see someone filming, I think the best thing to do is =
leave them alone.  You could say hello and ask them if they need any help o=
r directions. If they say no- then leave them alone.

I would be surprised if we see any of these folks...but if we do, they will=
 likely be outside on the sidewalks or parking lots and maybe even in the l=
obbies.

We don't want to end up on a YouTube channel about violating first amendmen=
t rights.  We do want to call our LEOs to notify them that there is a first=
 amendment auditor.



[Forest Service Shield]
Christina Ojeda
Volunteer Coordinator
Forest Service
Siuslaw National Forest
Oregon Dunes National Recreation Area
Central Coast Ranger District
p: 541-271-6016
c: 541-999-1838
christina.ojeda@usda.gov
                         855 Highway 101
                                      Reedsport, OR 97467










